":1,\"name\":\"In the Dark\",\"overview\":\"After a scary bedtime story, Sister Bear is too frightened of the dark to shut her eyes. But her parents give her some sound psychological advice and a night-light, that will help Sister conquer her fears.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-09-13\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"Ring the Bell\",\"overview\":\"At the Bear Country Fair, Too Tall Grizzly begins to taunt Brother Bear, resulting in a fight and is ended in a challenge of strength between Pa Bear and the formidable Two-Ton Grizzly.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-09-20\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Forget Their Manners\",\"overview\":\"Mama Bear decides to take her ill-mannered family in hand and offers them lessons to become polite, but she realizes that she received better luck from children than Papa. Unsuccessful in her method, she devises a Politeness Plan - a chart listing a chore as a penalty for each act of rudeness. The cubs foil the plan by being super polite and actually enjoy it.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-09-27\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"The Wicked Weasel Spell\",\"overview\":\"McGreedy Weasel and Raffish Ralph hypnotize Bigpaw Bear into attacking Bear Town. But, Brother and Sister break the spell in a flash. They know you can't make someone do something they really don't want to do!\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-10-04\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"The Truth\",\"overview\":\"On the loose, Brother and Sister defy Mama Bear's rule of only playing ball outside, by shattering Mama Bear's favorite lamp. Felling guilty, the two lie about it, but soon, with much coaxing and fact checking by Mama and Papa Bear, the cubs learn the importance of telling the truth.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-10-11\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"Save the Bees\",\"overview\":\"Raffish Ralph is chosen by Arch Weasel to create an ultimate weapon to take down Bear Country. They unleash a field of menacing honey bell flowers that threaten Bear Country's supply of honey, by engulfing all bees.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-05-27\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"Get in a Fight\",\"overview\":\"Brother and Sister get involved in a fight, that lasts all day long, and Mama Bear intervenes, revealing that everyone argues once in a while, even with loved ones.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-10-25\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"The Bigpaw Problem\",\"overview\":\"When Big Paw is arrested for being too big and clumsy, Big Paw receives the chance to save Bear Country from the effects of an earthquake, and he is declared a national treasure.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-11-01\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Get Stage Fright\",\"overview\":\"Sister Bear is feared that she will forget her lines when she is chosen to lead a school play. Despite Brother's teasing, she follows Mama's advice and practises until she's perfect. On the night of the performance, it's Brother who ends up with stage fright and who is rescued by his sympathetic sister.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-11-08\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":10,\"name\":\"Go Bonkers Over Honkers\",\"overview\":\"The Berenstain Bears Go Bonkers Over Honkers.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-11-15\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":11,\"name\":\"The Great Honey Pipeline\",\"overview\":\"After some convincing from Brother and Sister, Papa promises not to go after Wild Wild Honey anymore. But when Queen Nectar's honey supply goes missing, the Bear Detectives find Papa broke his word, so they recover the honey and give Papa a lesson he'll never forget.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-11-22\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":12,\"name\":\"The Great Grizzly Comet\",\"overview\":\"The Great Grizzly Comet is passing. Some \\\"little green bears\\\" arrive with a warning that the comet is on a collision course with Bear Country. Papa tells Farmer Ben, who both spread the alarm to evacuate Bear Country.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-11-29\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":13,\"name\":\"The Sure-Fire Bait\",\"overview\":\"Papa is determined to catch Old Jake the catfish.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-12-06\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":14,\"name\":\"The Cat's Meow\",\"overview\":\"Brother and Sister Bear are given the duty to look after Mrs. Honeybear's cat, Puff, while she's away on a trip with her family. Puff's unique meow leads the Berenstain Bears on quest to figure out why cat meow.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-12-13\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":15,\"name\":\"The Trouble With Friends\",\"overview\":\"A new Bear family arrives in a nearby treehouse, and Sister Bear finally finds a new friend who is around her age. Unfortunately, her new friend's tendency toward bossiness and bragging soon dampens their relationship.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-12-20\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":16,\"name\":\"The Coughing Catfish\",\"overview\":\"Jake the giant Catfish, among other animals are affected by garbage dumping in the lake. Brother and Sister get help from Professor Actual Factual to scan the extensive garbage pollution. Their solution is to use a sunken pirate ship as an attraction to fund cleanup projects.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1986-12-27\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":17,\"name\":\"The Substitute Teacher\",\"overview\":\"Brother, Cousin Freddy, and Too-Tall and his gang set up practical jokes for a substitute teacher, but they learn to like her when 